Salience is not a logical notion, though it enters in to this discussion at=
 some Gricean level.  But so far as logic goes, {lo} is just a function tha=
t returns an object from its range, the complex built on the extension of t=
he assigned predicate (a node in the upward semilattice of among applied to=
 the closure of the extension under part, according to the last guess I saw=
). It has no special properties, in other words, like uniqueness or specifi=
city or .... .  It has no logic of its own, as up and down do, though it ma=
y on occasion mimic at least down (some would say up, too, by I am unconvin=
ced). =20

Sent from my iPad

